  "graphicDesign": {
    "Overview": "Regarding graphic design and images, a common feature of grunge bands was the use of \"lo-fi\" (low fidelity) and deliberately unconventional album covers, for example presenting intentionally murky or miscolored photography, collage or distressed lettering. Early grunge \"[a]lbum covers and concert flyers appeared Xeroxed not in allegiance to some DIY aesthetic\" but because of \"economic necessity\", as \"bands had so little money\"."
  },
